.TH FIX_VIDEO 1 "October 2026" "fix_video 1.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fix_video \- automated audio dehum, de-crackle, and linear AV sync drift correction
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fix_video.sh
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIFILE\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fix_video.sh
is a high-performance shell utility for macOS and Linux designed to repair video and audio recordings corrupted by high-voltage electromagnetic interference (EMI) and asynchronous recording clock drift.
.PP
When filming under high-tension utility transmission lines, two major classes of audio corruption typically occur:
.IP 1. 4
\fBElectromagnetic Interference (Hum & Crackle):\fR A fundamental 60 Hz (or 50 Hz) sinusoidal current induces deep audible hum. Additionally, high-voltage corona discharges produce continuous microsecond electrical arcing impulses (crackle) and dense harmonic overtones (120 Hz through 600+ Hz) perceived as an intense frying or buzzing noise.
.IP 2. 4
\fBClock Misalignment (Linear Sync Drift):\fR Intense EMI can induce timing jitter in internal hardware clock crystals, causing audio and video sampling clocks to record at slightly different rates. Over a multi-minute recording, audio slowly leads or lags behind the video.
.PP
.B fix_video.sh
solves both problems in a single automated pass without generational video loss by passing the video stream through untouched (\fB\-c:v copy\fR) while applying a 5-stage digital signal processing (DSP) filtergraph to the audio track.

.SH DSP PIPELINE
The audio filtergraph is executed in the following strict order:
.TP
.B 1. Highpass Filter (\fIhighpass=f=80\fR)
Attenuates frequencies below 80 Hz with zero effect on human vocal fundamentals. Eliminates low-frequency electromagnetic mud, handling noise, and wind rumble.
.TP
.B 2. Impulsive Noise Filter (\fIadeclick\fR)
Scans for abrupt non-harmonic waveform discontinuities caused by electrostatic arcing and corona discharges. Interpolates corrupted samples prior to frequency domain processing.
.TP
.B 3. Adaptive Spectral Denoiser (\fIafftdn=nr=10:nf=\-45:tn=1\fR)
Applies Fast Fourier Transform (FFT) noise reduction with continuous real-time noise tracking to suppress the broadband induction floor.
.TP
.B 4. High-Q Harmonic Notch Filters (\fIbandreject\fR)
Applies sharp Butterworth band-reject filters with narrow Q-factor (\fIQ=30\fR) at the fundamental line frequency and all multiples through the 10th harmonic (60, 120, 180, 240, 300, 360, 420, 480, 540, 600 Hz).
.TP
.B 5. Dynamic Time Stretch (\fIatempo\fR)
Extracts exact container/stream durations down to the millisecond using \fBffprobe\fR, calculates the duration ratio using arbitrary-precision math (\fBbc\fR), and speeds or slows the audio to match the video duration without shifting pitch.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display summary help text and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry-run
Probe streams, calculate the speed stretch ratio, and print the resulting filtergraph without executing audio re-encoding.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIPATH\fR"
Explicit path for output file. By default, appends \fI_fixed\fR to the input filename in the same directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-highpass " HZ"
Set the cutoff frequency for sub-rumble highpass filter in Hz (default: 80). Pass 0 to disable.
.TP
.BI \-\-q-factor " Q"
Set the Q-factor for harmonic notch filters (default: 30). Higher values produce narrower notches, preserving surrounding vocal content.
.TP
.BI \-\-harmonics " N"
Number of harmonics to notch starting from the base frequency (default: 10, i.e. 60 Hz to 600 Hz).
.TP
.BI \-\-base-freq " HZ"
Fundamental power grid frequency in Hz (default: 60 for North America; set to 50 for European 50 Hz power grids).
.TP
.B \-\-no-declick
Disable stage 2 impulsive de-clicking.
.TP
.B \-\-no-denoise
Disable stage 3 adaptive FFT noise suppression.

.SH ENVIRONMENT & DEPENDENCIES
Requires standard macOS or Linux POSIX environment with:
.TP
.B ffmpeg
Audio/video multiplexing and DSP filtering engine.
.TP
.B ffprobe
Stream header duration extractor.
.TP
.B bc
Arbitrary precision floating point calculator.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. Output file written.
.TP
.B 1
Error (missing arguments, missing input file, or missing dependencies).

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Standard automated repair:
.RS
.B ./fix_video.sh /Users/mike/ai/dehum/VID_20261009_111445043.mp4
.RE
.PP
Preview stream ratio and filter chain:
.RS
.B ./fix_video.sh \-\-dry\-run input.mp4
.RE
.PP
Process European 50 Hz recording:
.RS
.B ./fix_video.sh \-\-base\-freq 50 \-\-harmonics 8 input.mp4
.RE

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR ffprobe (1),
.BR bc (1)
